      "itemDescription": "In CEO David Long\u2019s final year at the helm, the privately owned global property and casualty insurer dropped eight spots on the Fortune 500.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>After Long retired at the end of 2022, the company\u2019s board appointed Liberty Mutual veteran Timothy Sweeney as CEO in January 2023.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In 2022, the 111-year-old insurer, based in Boston, saw an 87% decrease in year-over-year profit and a modest gain in revenue of 4%.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>Liberty Mutual, along with more than a dozen other insurers, continues to push back against the Boy Scouts\u2019 record $2.46 billion settlement of sexual abuse allegations that obligates the insurers to pay what they say are \"invalid and questionable claims.\"</li><br />\r\n</ul>",
